# Meridian Front: a sci-fi real-time strategy campaign invented as a genre example. No game's
# names, data or logic. A fleet fights its way across four planets, one chapter each. Missions
# open from a war room in a tree; each mission has three objectives, and each objective is a
# check. Items are planet coordinates (they open a chapter), unit types and upgrades.
world meridian_front "Meridian Front" version 1
use army
use campaign
use finales
start war_room

# How long the campaign is: the chapters past this one are left out, missions and all.
option chapters: range 2..4 = 4
# Side operations are optional missions off the main line.
option side_ops: toggle = on
# `campaign` keeps the mission tree; `open` lets any mission of a planet you can reach be
# played in any order.
option mission_order: choice(campaign, open) = campaign

# The first planet's coordinates and the basic infantry are there from the start.
start_item halvar_coordinates
start_item trooper

# The campaign is won when the finale of each chapter in play is won.
goal counter(chapter_won) >= opt.chapters
